OpenBSD FVWM 2.2.5: Core Program Rewrite
=========================================

Changes to the main fvwm window manager, its headers, and config.

  config.h:        Rewrote for OpenBSD-only (48 autoconf probes removed)
  fvwm.c:          Privilege separation, staged pledge(2)/unveil(2)
  builtins.c:      Fixed double-free, exit()->_exit(), pointer aliasing,
                   putenv() leak, typo; removed shell comment
  module.c:        Fixed negative-size text[-1] write (CRITICAL),
                   exit()->_exit(), wrong strlcpy size
  modconf.c:       Fixed NULL pointer arithmetic in DestroyModConfig
  read.c:          Added recursion depth guard (MAX_NESTING_DEPTH=128)
  style.c:         Fixed uninitialized error-message buffer
  events.c:        Removed commented-out CLICKY_MODE_1 #ifdef/#endif
  add_window.c:    Replaced vague TODO with precise limitation description
  colormaps.c:     Removed Sun/Solaris TrueColor workaround
  misc.h:          Removed waitpid(2)/wait3(2) branching, __STDC__ guards
  move.c:          Added ClampToScreen() for Escape/abort during moves
  fvwm2.1:         Rewrote man page in semantic mdoc(7) (3041->369 lines)
  Makefile:        Added exec.c, fvwm_exec target, -lutil

  NEW: exec.c              Main-process imsg(3) interface to exec helper
  NEW: fvwm_exec.c         Privilege-separated execution helper
  NEW: fvwm_sandbox.h      Shared pledge(2)/unveil(2) inline helpers
  NEW: xalloc.h            xmalloc/xrealloc/xcalloc/xstrdup inline helpers

Apply with:  patch -p0 < 0001-core-rewrite.patch
From the CVS repository root directory containing fvwm/

NOT VERIFIED: No compilation or runtime testing performed.

